        coreEn: "A-side: The reverse of cosmic horror is cosmic awe — though tiny, you are the only part of this universe that can 'realize it's tiny.' Your consciousness itself is the miracle. / B-side: Collapse of human narrative — everything about 'nation,' 'family,' 'career,' 'love' is a bacterium on a dust mote narrating its own epic before 13.7 billion years. Key tension: If you're completely unimportant to the universe — do you still have reason to live? | Real punctured: You don't 'live in the universe' — you ARE the universe. You're one way the universe observes itself.",
        reference: "洛夫克拉夫特创造的克苏鲁神话中面对不可名状之物时理智崩溃的人类；《2001太空漫游》中飞向木星后进入光之隧道的宇航员。",
        referenceEn: "Humans whose sanity breaks facing the unnamable in Lovecraft's Cthulhu Mythos; the astronaut entering the light tunnel after flying toward Jupiter in 2001: A Space Odyssey.",

        topology: "人类叙事的崩解：不是'很大'——而是你的一切故事在137亿年面前就像灰尘上的细菌在讲述史诗",

